        ["Which outcome measure is MOST appropriate for a patient with upper extremity dysfunction?", ["QuickDASH", "Oswestry Disability Index", "Lower Extremity Functional Scale", "Berg Balance Scale"], "QuickDASH measures upper extremity function. Oswestry is for low back pain; LEFS is for lower extremity."],
        ["A student is consistently 20 minutes behind by midday. Which change is MOST likely to help?", ["Plan each session in advance and document at point of service", "Shorten each patient's session by 10 minutes", "Skip documentation until the end of the day", "Ask the PTA to evaluate the new patients"], "Planning and point-of-service documentation improve flow. Skipping notes or delegating evaluations is inappropriate."],
        ["A student wants to cover a new patient's evaluation without discussing it with the CI before the patient leaves. What is the BEST practice?", ["Briefly review the diagnosis, plan, and HEP with the CI first", "Send the CI a summary at the end of the day", "Wait for the CI to review the note next week", "Ask the patient to describe the visit to the CI"], "A brief review before the patient leaves catches errors while they can still be corrected."],
        ["A 60-year-old patient with back pain mentions a 7 kg unexplained weight loss and a history of prostate cancer. What is the MOST appropriate action?", ["Inform the CI and refer to the physician before continuing", "Treat for mechanical back pain and monitor weight", "Ask the patient to follow up at the next annual exam", "Provide a home program and reassess in four weeks"], "Unexplained weight loss with cancer history is a red flag for metastatic disease that requires medical referral."],
        ["Which statement BEST describes expected caseload growth in an outpatient rotation?", ["Gradual increase from partial to a near-full caseload", "Full caseload from the first day of the rotation", "Observation only for the first half of the rotation", "Evaluations only with no follow-up patients"], "Caseload builds progressively, with independence increasing toward the end."],
        ["A student documents that a patient's shoulder 'improved,' without numbers. What is MOST important to add?", ["Objective measures compared with baseline", "The patient's insurance information", "A list of all exercises done at home", "The CI's opinion of the patient's attitude"], "Progress must be shown with objective data compared with baseline values."]
